        "payload": "tree c337619c8f419b1dd7da572a784e2e0ebf730f50\nparent 740423ed5b6922611c73ec804bfcf061252ef5fb\nauthor matthew bradley <168114+mbradley@users.noreply.github.com> 1779488070 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779488070 -0400\n\nfix(moderate): route ban/unban through NIP-86 and correct method names (#88)\n\n* fix(moderate): route ban/unban through NIP-86 and use correct method names\n\nban_pubkey published a kind 10000 event via WebSocket which the relay\naccepted but never processed as a management command. Refactored to use\nhandleRelayRpc (HTTP POST with NIP-98 auth), matching the delete_event\npattern that already works.\n\nallow_pubkey/allowevent sent method names that Funnelcake accepts\nsilently but does not act on. Changed to unbanpubkey/unbanevent which\nare the methods Funnelcake actually implements.\n\nFixes divinevideo/support-trust-safety#147\n\n* fix: remove duplicate DM, restore markHumanReviewed on unban, clean dead code\n\n- ban_pubkey: remove DM notification (handleRelayRpc already sends it)\n- allow_pubkey: restore markHumanReviewed (dropped during refactor)\n- Remove unreachable finalizeEvent/publishToRelay block after switch\n\n* test: fix WebSocket mock for vitest 4.x compatibility\n\nArrow functions cannot be called with `new` (JS language constraint).\nVitest 4.x tightened mockImplementation to actually invoke the mock\nas a constructor, so the arrow function threw TypeError. Switching to\na function expression fixes it. Broken since the vitest 4 upgrade.\n\n* fix: address review feedback on restore, audit, and kind-5 publish\n\n- Filter restore actions by per-hash status so Unblock only clears\n  blocked hashes and Remove Restriction only clears restricted hashes\n- Add logDecision audit row to profile-card delete path with reportId\n- Publish kind-5 deletion events via WebSocket with OK confirmation\n  instead of HTTP POST that relays don't accept",
