  {
    "sha": "e9bdc7a359fe4cae9f0c892733e7d71e8d64b96d",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOQjhVC9oAKGU5YmRjN2EzNTlmZTRjYWU5ZjBjODkyNzMzZTdkNzFlOGQ2NGI5NmQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "matthew bradley",
        "email": "168114+mbradley@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-05-22T13:33:42Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "GitHub",
        "email": "noreply@github.com",
        "date": "2026-05-22T13:33:42Z"
      },
      "message": "fix: dedup report categories, surface Keycast failures, audit partial deletes (#82)\n\n* refactor: deduplicate getReportCategory and HIGH_PRIORITY_CATEGORIES in Reports.tsx (#81)\n\nReplace local getReportCategory and HIGH_PRIORITY_CATEGORIES with\nimports from src/lib/constants.ts. The local HIGH_PRIORITY_CATEGORIES\nwas missing NS-underageUser and NS-childSafety, so child-safety\nreports were not getting priority treatment in the queue list view.\n\nCloses #81\n\n* fix: surface Keycast enforcement failures and audit partial deletes\n\nAddress two pre-existing issues flagged during review:\n\n1. AgeReviewDetail: when case state transitions to restricted/cleared/denied,\n   the worker returns keycastUpdated in the response. Previously the UI\n   ignored this flag, showing success even when account enforcement failed.\n   Now shows a destructive toast when keycastUpdated is false.\n\n2. EventActions: deleteEventAndMediaMutation ran four sequential steps\n   with a single audit log at the end. If media deletion or logging failed\n   after the event was already destroyed, the error toast hid what succeeded\n   and the audit trail was incomplete. Now logs each irreversible side effect\n   immediately and surfaces partial success to the moderator.",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "7a242da9f2bad6405ee9c874a99cec054a360518",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/divinevideo/divine-relay-manager/git/trees/7a242da9f2bad6405ee9c874a99cec054a360518"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/divinevideo/divine-relay-manager/git/commits/e9bdc7a359fe4cae9f0c892733e7d71e8d64b96d",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqEFs2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7scQAI8sDM6rEecvTJ67Nv26KfR5\n40tW3HooiQhaB13G7217nwOrg3yVqLeWKTMGAq61qwEr9cfKqI8ohZCwava8Vy2O\nEXe2fJKjGa4/Ve6IS/I1Xn9InGuVnkkyk7LzyWK3iZAuLDKFkoWPjr705/fKR0O/\nHTpMcWj3ep6RP8KCcae7cqrdM0mVAn7NZv/ZHy6y4BQj6Bxa40/JDMDUcf6RcSld\nyKh1v5N9BaFYq2dsor1/ERgAPT7cWezZ5HPnaW2lwaPqBS+za5SXaR7x+WjA0rqe\nxTykedcllyCaAfXRsSDsbMVkwPTQGw6T1AoPwvsu7ZzwY9xgmO/coHqim25EniO5\nUr7TNCqMRX5LJKnpajRWql9DCA6nE7h8EQihxwGEBfzAq0ld3I/FWsR93tteek6p\ntSlgt94XHuzrjTE+7abGkTl+jb3bklk4wAq1P24IiIpC6WaCsaeRZ5wIfXetwDgN\nO2tB1hWnhi6XwxH4xO364YFB0OUvv9qLMVw5X2FhDJKtHH/1kebD3+iY5FgHXlx9\nTSEsO/aCf759P1YDnDJ9HJlic9vAtGuYmovKIKKnKocnXQpgmiSQ79DalV2ttFwc\nBv5Bt5VUvc3XuifQrbVXwsPTmy8P3+jfRFNuwC/qodv/ZIsTIBzvAi2y976h5HjO\nrkDH+x7+PRyrbD9rConJ\n=V727\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree 7a242da9f2bad6405ee9c874a99cec054a360518\nparent 2a9a2d69702eb5ed7d167cf8c895b6a2827dcfd6\nauthor matthew bradley <168114+mbradley@users.noreply.github.com> 1779456822 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779456822 -0400\n\nfix: dedup report categories, surface Keycast failures, audit partial deletes (#82)\n\n* refactor: deduplicate getReportCategory and HIGH_PRIORITY_CATEGORIES in Reports.tsx (#81)\n\nReplace local getReportCategory and HIGH_PRIORITY_CATEGORIES with\nimports from src/lib/constants.ts. The local HIGH_PRIORITY_CATEGORIES\nwas missing NS-underageUser and NS-childSafety, so child-safety\nreports were not getting priority treatment in the queue list view.\n\nCloses #81\n\n* fix: surface Keycast enforcement failures and audit partial deletes\n\nAddress two pre-existing issues flagged during review:\n\n1. AgeReviewDetail: when case state transitions to restricted/cleared/denied,\n   the worker returns keycastUpdated in the response. Previously the UI\n   ignored this flag, showing success even when account enforcement failed.\n   Now shows a destructive toast when keycastUpdated is false.\n\n2. EventActions: deleteEventAndMediaMutation ran four sequential steps\n   with a single audit log at the end. If media deletion or logging failed\n   after the event was already destroyed, the error toast hid what succeeded\n   and the audit trail was incomplete. Now logs each irreversible side effect\n   immediately and surfaces partial success to the moderator.",
        "verified_at": "2026-05-22T13:33:43Z"
      }
